Chapter: PunctualTextAppend

 A punctual function that concatenates text. The append allocates, so
 it must be rejected with CDX6002. The check matched OpAppend, which
 only the show-of-a-record desugaring ever builds; the & token
 desugars to OpAnd and is separated from logical and by the operand
 type alone, so every one of these compiled clean and collected an
 affirmative CDX6010 certificate.

Section: Definitions

  punctual bad-label : Text -> Text
  bad-label (t) = t & "!"

  punctual bad-prefix : Text -> Text
  bad-prefix (t) = "[" & t

  punctual bad-join : Text, Text -> Text
  bad-join (a) (b) = a & b

  opening : Integer = 0
